  "description": {
    "text": "Two jumbo cards numbered with a J suffix, released alongside the P promos from August 2001 to July 2002: the smallest numbered Japanese promo set. Timeless Celebi came with the September 2001 issue of CoroCoro Comic, out in August 2001, and Latias and Latios with the theatrical release of the film Guardian Gods of the City of Water: Latias and Latios. Later jumbo cards often carry just the black star PROMO symbol, and more recent ones the suffix of the promo set of their day with no number.",
    "sources": [
      {
        "title": "Bulbapedia: J Promotional cards (TCG) (Wayback Machine copy, 10 March 2026)",
        "url": "https://web.archive.org/web/20260310030220/https://bulbapedia.bulbagarden.net/wiki/%22J%22_Promotional_cards_(TCG)"
      }
    ]
  },
  "tell": {
    "text": "A black star symbol at the right, and a \"/J\" number",
