      "description": {
        "text": "A jumbo card given out at cinemas showing Guardian Gods of the City of Water: Latias and Latios, the fifth Pokémon film, which opened in Japan on 13 July 2002 and came out in English as Pokémon Heroes. Its top line calls it a cinema-only jumbo card for the fifth anniversary of Pikachu the Movie, whose logo is printed at the bottom.\n\nLatias and Latios fly past four circles holding Celebi, Mewtwo, Entei and Lugia, and no illustrator is credited. Its one attack lets you take any of the Pokémon in the circles from your own collection and put them onto your Bench, even when it is full. Its text says those four appear somewhere in the film in another form, gives a hint (look at the tiles of the secret garden's floor), and sends readers to the film's website for the answer. It is the second of the two J promos, jumbo cards numbered as promos, after Timeless Celebi 001/J.",
        "sources": [
          {
            "title": "Pokumon: Latias and Latios (002/J Japanese Promo)",
